#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# cuboid

#% text
# `cuboid(pmin, pmax)` is the box with opposite corners pmin and pmax in `graphics3d`.

#% text
# `cuboid([x, y, z])` is the unit cube with its lowest corner there; `cuboid()` at the origin.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Coordinates are in the units of the graphic; the box around the scene follows the data unless `plot_range` says otherwise.

#% item
# Colours, `opacity` and `edge_form` before it in its list style it; faces are lit.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# The default:

#% cell
graphics3d(cuboid())
#% output
#= image("cuboid.files/cuboid-1.png")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A row of cubes:

#% cell
graphics3d(table([hue(k/5), cuboid([1.5k, 0, 0])], k, 5))
#% output
#= image("cuboid.files/cuboid-2.png")

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# A long box seen from the front:

#% cell
graphics3d(cuboid([0, 0, 0], [3, 1, 1]), view_point: front)
#% output
#= image("cuboid.files/cuboid-3.png")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `graphics3d`, `sphere`, `plot3d`
